      "bio": "Jared Evan Moskowitz (/ˈmɒskəwɪts/ MOSS-kə-wits; born December 18, 1980) is an American politician serving as the U.S. representative for Florida's 23rd congressional district since 2023. A member of the Democratic Party, he previously served on the Broward County Commission from 2022 to 2023 and as director of the Florida Division of Emergency Management from 2019 to 2021. Moskowitz also represented the Coral Springs-Parkland area in the Florida House of Representatives from 2012 to 2019.",
      "campaign_website": "http://moskowitz.house.gov",
      "key_messages": [
        "Moskowitz strongly supports Israel and opposes pro-Palestine activism, voting for aid to Israel and criticizing demonstrations he views as anti-Semitic while opposing the ICC arrest warrant for Netanyahu.",
        "Moskowitz supports stricter immigration enforcement, joining Republicans and 45 other House Democrats in voting for the Laken Riley Act in 2025.",
        "Moskowitz supports government efficiency and reorganizing federal agencies, being the only Democrat to join the Department of Government Efficiency (DOGE) caucus and proposing to reduce the size of the Department of Homeland Security.",
        "Moskowitz voted to fund Israel aid by cutting the IRS budget rather than other means of funding."
      ],
